    description: "Stop hook watched-process detection over-matches: pgrep -af \"pytest|...\" treats any cmdline containing \"pytest\" as a live watched process, including inotifywait helpers invoked with /tmp/pytest-.../ path args. The existing filter at stop_logic.sh:237-240 only strips bash -c/sh -c wrappers. Result: hook sleeps up to 30 min (WATCHED_MAX_WAIT_SECS=1800) waiting on leaked inotifywait processes (observed etime 1h+ from pytest-952), blocking the user's session until they hit Esc. Fix: anchor detection to argv[0] basename (after path strip) instead of substring match on full cmdline. WI-varid introduced the process-aware pause but did not scope the detection."  # 4189
    fields: {}  # 4189
